WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.000
Welcome to "The Tonight Show." Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.501
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.434
♪♪

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:11.767
Well, guys, today, the C.E.O. of Pfizer said that

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:15.534
its vaccine for the Omicron variant will be ready in March.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.167
So get ready for the craziest St. Patrick's Day

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.601
in the history of the world.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.734
[Irish accent] Omicron!

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.200
[Normal voice] Pretty soon, the C.E.O. of Pfizer

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.834
is going to be on Instagram Live like,

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:27.901
"New vaccine just dropped.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:31.334
Sound off in the comments! What?!"

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:32.868
It feels like this March Madness,

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.667
we'll be filling out brackets to predict

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.300
which of the 68 variants become the dominant strain.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.667
Listen to this.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:43.234
According to the CDC, only 1 in 10 adults in the U.S.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.200
eat enough fruits and vegetables.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.100
Good timing on this news, CDC.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.334
It sort of feels like their version of

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.334
"Hey, what's over there?"

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.434
"There's a bird. Look, there's a bird."

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.234
Yep, the CDC says adults should eat 2 to 3 cups

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.968
of vegetables a day.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.934
Wait. Now they're saying 4 to 5.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.300
No, wait. No, now they're saying only 1.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.234
Basically, barely 1 or 2. You're fine with 1.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.267
Yeah, we'll figure it out.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.601
I heard that Tesla's self-driving program

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:14.434
now offers three different modes that control behaviors,

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.000
like rolling stops, running yellow lights,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.234
and how close you are to follow other drivers.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.434
And they have three modes.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:23.734
They're called Chill, Average, and Assertive.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.634
And this is fun.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:29.567
You can also hit Mood Swing and try all three at random.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.434
And I also heard that some Honda and Acura models

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:37.534
have been hit with a bug that resets their clocks

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:40.000
20 years in the past.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.701
The company could tell something was up

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.868
when drivers seemed happy.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:47.767
It's crazy. People were driving along.

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:48.901
Then, all of a sudden,

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.934
the radio would only play the Goo Goo Dolls.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.534
Yeah. Get this.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:56.534
I saw that nearly 15,000 pounds of Walmart beef sticks

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.767
have been recalled because they forgot to label

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.901
a potential allergen.

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:03.501
Yep, Walmart beef sticks must now have a label

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:07.133
that says "Warning -- you're eating Walmart beef sticks."

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:08.901
Oh.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:12.033
-Oh. Oh, okay. -Yeah.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.701
Apparently, a supermarket chain in the U.K. is getting rid of

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.167
the "use by" dates on its milk

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:20.434
and encouraging customers to use the sniff test.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.501
Yep, here's how it works in every house.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:26.067
You grab a carton and immediately go,

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.033
"Honey, does this smell bad to you?"

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.868
And, finally, a farmer in Turkey is having his cows

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:35.300
wear V.R. goggles that simulate green pastures

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.300
so that they'll be less anxious.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.434
Take a look at this.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:41.334
It's real.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:42.968
Yeah, the cow doesn't make any more milk,

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:47.567
but it is really good at the new game "Beef Saber."

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.567
Well, guys, today, New York -- New York City got slammed

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:53.000
with an Arctic blast, causing wind chills

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.067
around zero degrees, making it one of New York City's

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.067
coldest day in years. Yep.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:02:59.567
You can't see it at home, but right now,

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.300
the entire audience is spooning each other.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:08.367
Today, even the biggest anti-maskers are like,

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.901
"Damn it! Give me one. All right."

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:12.634
"Give me an N95, too."

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:13.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.968
Yeah, it's that type of cold where the Domino's guy

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.734
sits on your pizza while delivering it.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:18.868
You know -- You know what I'm saying?

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.934
-Aww! [ Laughter ]

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.534
Eee! -Well, this is exciting.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.934
I saw that the Girl Scouts announced a new partnership

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.367
with DoorDash, that will allow their drivers

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.567
to deliver Girl Scout cookies.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.234
[ Cheers ] Yeah.

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:34.367
Right now, there's a bunch of 50-year-old drivers like,

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.133
"Do I really have to wear the sash?"

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.000
"All right, I'll give it a go." [ Laughter ]

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.234
I don't know. Is it really buying

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.000
Girl Scout cookies if you're not guilted

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.167
into ordering as many boxes as your co-workers?

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:53.501
"Really, Kelly bought 10 boxes. Just saying."

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:55.868
If you're keeping track, we can't get rapid tests

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.234
to Americans, but Do-Si-Dos? Check.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.634
We figured that out.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.434
Hey, this is fun. The TSA just released

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:06.400
its annual list of the weirdest things that they've confiscated.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.734
And this year's items include a chainsaw

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.567
and a burrito filled with meth.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.200
-Whoa! -Yep.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.167
Someone tried flying with a chainsaw.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:21.234
In fairness, how else can you cut through

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.367
the chicken on a United flight? [ Laughter ]

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:27.834
[ Imitating chainsaw running ]

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.067
"Looks a little tough. You want a bite of my burrito?"

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.801
Well, the pandemic has caused all kinds of shortages

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.934
around the world, but Norway's military

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.701
is dealing with a very unique one.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:39.968
Check this out.

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:43.167
-Norway's military faces an extraordinary problem --

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.367
a shortage of undergarments.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.501
At the end of their service, recruits must now

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.133
turn in their underwear, bras, and socks

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:53.734
so that the next group of servicemembers can reuse them.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.200
-Oh. [ Laughter ]

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.501
Ew!

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:01.367
-Whether it's the Norwegian military or Norwegian Cruises,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.834
they have the same slogan --

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.334
"You're gonna need extra underwear."

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:08.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:11.467
I think this is why the military invented "going commando."

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:12.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:17.000
What's that? A lifetime achievement award?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.767
That's fantastic. Thank --

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.901
Oh, you're not airing it on TV or streaming it?

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:22.200
Oh, okay. I won't say anything.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.667
But, anyways, thank you very much.

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:25.234
No, thank you. Thank you.

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.367
-Wow. [ Laughter ]

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.334
For those two jokes. -Amazing. Yeah.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.334
Just for that one, I think. -Just for the one joke?

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:31.534
The commando joke? -Yeah.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.667
-Man, good for you. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.534
-No, no, not cool.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:36.901
♪♪

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.667
Thank you very much. Hey, guys, get this.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:41.934
Hulk Hogan's under a lot of fire after he suggested

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:43.868
that the COVID vaccine is to blame

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:47.267
for the recent deaths of some of our biggest celebrities.

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:49.000
As a result, Hulk Hogan has been named

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.834
the heavyweight champion of Facebook.

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.601
Yeah, you're laughing now, but if Trump's re-elected,

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:56.367
he's the new Dr. Fauci.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.167
There was a new episode of "The Bachelor" last night.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:02.634
You guys watch "The Bachelor"?

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:04.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:07.100
There was a pretty dramatic scene between two women,

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.601
Shanae and Elizabeth.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.534
Now, the show can get pretty emotional,

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.334
and I thought that we could help.

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:15.133
Here's that moment re-voiced with the least emotional person

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:16.767
we know, Siri.

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:19.567
This is, "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:24.200
[ Applause ]

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.167
-I thought you and I were on the same page yesterday.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:27.834
-We were not on the same page yesterday.

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:30.167
-So, is it you're ADHD,

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.901
or is it me that you have a problem with?

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:34.100
-I think this is really inappropriate, Shanae.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.767
-So, are you telling everyone in the house you have ADHD?

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.434
-You already brought it to the attention of the girls.

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:39.133
-I didn't tell anyone you have ADHD.

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.334
I have ADHD. -You absolutely did tell.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.234
-I mean, [bleep] little kids have ADHD.

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:44.434
-Okay.

00:06:44.434 --> 00:06:46.300
-And I think you're using that as an excuse.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.467
-I really don't appreciate how you're coming at me,

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:50.367
and if you'd like to apologize to me, I'll do so,

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:51.801
but, unfortunately, I'm not going to engage

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:53.100
in this conversation with you anymore.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.367
-Okay. Well, I'm just saying,

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:56.367
like, I have ADHD, too.

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:57.634
-Wow.

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:59.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:03.601
-Very -- A lot of drama there.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:05.033
Well, some more entertainment news.

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:07.767
ABC just announced that, after a three-year hiatus,

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:10.400
this year's Oscars will have a host.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.467
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.334
Unfortunately, it's Hulk Hogan. -Oh.

00:07:13.334 --> 00:07:15.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:21.200
"The Oscar, brother, goes --"

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.701
Did you guys hear about this?

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:26.234
A federal judge just ruled that U.S. cheese makers

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:28.234
can still make gruyere cheese

00:07:28.234 --> 00:07:32.033
even if it doesn't come from the Gruyere region of Switzerland.

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:35.133
Yep. However, the judge said Velveeta still must come from

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:37.834
the Velveeta region of France.

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:40.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:42.868
[ Rimshot ]

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:45.868
France -- France, New Jersey.

00:07:45.868 --> 00:07:47.868
That's right. [ Laughter ]

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:49.801
Hey, if this cheese case is appealed,

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:52.567
it could be heard by the Nacho Supreme Court.

00:07:52.567 --> 00:07:54.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:55.801
What's that? I'm sorry. What?

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:56.868
Hold on a second.

00:07:56.868 --> 00:07:58.534
Another lifetime achievement award?

00:07:58.534 --> 00:08:00.400
[ Laughter ] This is unbelievable.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.834
This one will stream. Oh, my gosh.

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:04.601
So people will -- It's on Quibi.

00:08:04.601 --> 00:08:06.601
Okay. Well, thank you very much.

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:08.000
I appreciate it. Thank you so much.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.534
Wow. [ Laughter ]

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.734
You won't believe -- What a night I've had.

00:08:11.734 --> 00:08:13.868
-Wow. [ Laughter ]

00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:17.300
-Finally, a woman in Canada was just reunited with her cat

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.701
when it turned up at her shelter 12 years after going missing.

00:08:20.701 --> 00:08:22.133
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:23.801
Meanwhile, the cat was like, "What the hell do I have to do

00:08:23.801 --> 00:08:26.067
to get away from this lady?"

00:08:26.067 --> 00:08:29.234
Today is National Pharmacist Day.

00:08:29.234 --> 00:08:32.067
Yeah. To celebrate, pharmacists everywhere were like,

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:34.567
"A Pfizer shot for you and a tequila shot for me.

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:36.634
Here we go. Let's keep it going."

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:38.501
If you want to do something nice for your pharmacist,

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:40.267
you can stop asking them if they have any more

00:08:40.267 --> 00:08:41.567
COVID tests in the back.

00:08:41.567 --> 00:08:44.801
"Everything we have is out."

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.701
Speaking of COVID tests, the State of Florida

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:52.400
let a million COVID tests expire in a warehouse.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:57.067
But now the FDA has decided to extend the expiration dates.

00:08:57.067 --> 00:08:58.234
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.334
When they heard that, every New York hot-dog vendor

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:07.701
was like, "Is that really safe to do that?

00:09:07.701 --> 00:09:09.100
Because..."

00:09:11.567 --> 00:09:14.000
Yeah, the FDA just extended the expiration dates.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.968
When they heard that, the CDC said,

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:18.901
"Hey, making up rules as you go is our thing."

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:21.767
Meanwhile, Florida was like, "You can put any date

00:09:21.767 --> 00:09:22.801
on them if you want.

00:09:22.801 --> 00:09:23.868
We're still not going to use them.

00:09:23.868 --> 00:09:25.601
We don't care. We don't..."

00:09:25.601 --> 00:09:26.667
Now, get this.

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:28.801
I saw that grade schools in Massachusetts

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.868
are using dogs to sniff out COVID.

00:09:31.868 --> 00:09:33.767
So if the dog starts barking,

00:09:33.767 --> 00:09:36.667
either you have COVID or Lunchables.

00:09:39.801 --> 00:09:42.934
[ Sniffs, growls ]

00:09:42.934 --> 00:09:44.534
-"Bologna." -But good news.

00:09:44.534 --> 00:09:47.534
If this works, The White House plans to mail everyone

00:09:47.534 --> 00:09:48.934
in the U.S. a COVID dog.

00:09:48.934 --> 00:09:51.067
That's right. So that's kind of cool.

00:09:51.067 --> 00:09:53.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.868
Yesterday, former President Trump

00:09:56.868 --> 00:09:59.834
hung up during an interview with NPR.

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:04.100
[As Trump] I've had enough.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.033
[Normal voice] After being challenged on

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:07.634
his baseless election-fraud claims.

00:10:07.634 --> 00:10:09.200
Of course, it's not the first time

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.634
Trump's hung up on a phone call.

00:10:10.634 --> 00:10:13.367
I mean, we actually got ahold of some audio from other ones.

00:10:13.367 --> 00:10:15.167
-Really? -Yeah. Take a listen to these.

00:10:36.267 --> 00:10:39.200
Very interesting. It's just -- -Wow!

00:10:40.167 --> 00:10:42.767
-Quick to the trigger on that. -Wow!

00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:46.868
-Switching gears, researchers found that Netflix

00:10:46.868 --> 00:10:50.834
has continued to produce content that shows people smoking,

00:10:50.834 --> 00:10:53.567
despite making a pledge that they would stop.

00:10:53.567 --> 00:10:56.801
Yeah, people don't want Netflix to glorify addiction

00:10:56.801 --> 00:10:59.834
while they watch five hours of Netflix every night.

00:11:03.734 --> 00:11:05.968
Netflix was like, "We had a doll mow down

00:11:05.968 --> 00:11:07.267
300 people in 'Squid Game.'

00:11:07.267 --> 00:11:10.501
You're drawing the line at smoking? Okay."

00:11:10.834 --> 00:11:12.000
Well, listen to this.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.934
I saw that the Oscars are going to have a host

00:11:13.934 --> 00:11:16.100
for the first time in four years.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.200
Yeah, that will be great. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:20.334 --> 00:11:21.567
Well, it turns out a lot of celebrities

00:11:21.567 --> 00:11:23.100
are interested in the job, and we actually got

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.534
our hands on some leaked audio of their auditions.

00:11:25.534 --> 00:11:26.767
Here, take a look at this.

00:11:26.767 --> 00:11:28.767
-Oh, man. [ Chuckles ]

00:11:28.767 --> 00:11:31.400
I can't believe I'm hosting the Oscars right now.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:33.734
This is so crazy.

00:11:33.734 --> 00:11:37.667
Okay, so, like, here are the nominees for Best Kiss?

00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:40.901
Oh, no! I don't think that's an award.

00:11:40.901 --> 00:11:42.434
Kissing's, like, pretty tight, though.

00:11:42.434 --> 00:11:43.434
[ Beep ]

00:11:43.434 --> 00:11:44.801
-Oh, wow! -Wow!

00:11:44.801 --> 00:11:48.167
-Wow! This is just -- Look at these bright lights.

00:11:48.167 --> 00:11:51.067
-Oh, my God! Those little statues! Wow!

00:11:51.067 --> 00:11:52.601
-Wow! -Wow!

00:11:52.601 --> 00:11:53.934
-Wow! [ Beep ]

00:11:53.934 --> 00:11:56.033
-Great to be here on Hollywood's biggest night, brother.

00:11:56.033 --> 00:11:59.667
I read on Facebook that wireless printers give you COVID,

00:11:59.667 --> 00:12:02.133
also those Applebee's buzzers, too.

00:12:02.133 --> 00:12:03.467
Anyways, the nominees for

00:12:03.467 --> 00:12:06.834
Best Technical Direction in a Short Film are, brother...

00:12:06.834 --> 00:12:08.334
Oh, wow. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:12.367 --> 00:12:14.200
"Wow!" -"Wow!"

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.300
-Some business news.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.734
Apparently, DIRECTV and Dish Network

00:12:17.734 --> 00:12:20.234
are once again in talks to merge.

00:12:20.234 --> 00:12:22.000
Yeah, it's taken a while to reach a deal

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.567
because neither of them work when it's raining.

00:12:25.868 --> 00:12:28.634
That's right -- DIRECTV and Dish Network might merge,

00:12:28.634 --> 00:12:30.834
and if they do, maybe they'll be named

00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:33.501
Forbes' Most Powerful Company of 2003.

00:12:33.501 --> 00:12:35.234
Hey, I heard that Domino's said, this year,

00:12:35.234 --> 00:12:39.100
it's expecting unprecedented food-cost increases.

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.367
Meanwhile, Papa John's was like,

00:12:40.367 --> 00:12:42.667
"As long as ketchup prices stay low, we're fine."

00:12:42.667 --> 00:12:44.934
[ Audience groans ]

00:12:44.934 --> 00:12:47.934
Oh, come on. He's not watching. [ Laughter ]

00:12:47.934 --> 00:12:49.634
And, finally, a pub owner in Ireland

00:12:49.634 --> 00:12:51.367
is so tired of hearing about COVID

00:12:51.367 --> 00:12:53.567
that he's making any customer who mentions the virus

00:12:53.567 --> 00:12:56.567
put 2 euros in the COVID jar.

00:12:56.567 --> 00:12:59.067
Yeah, that's not to be confused with the other COVID jar,

00:12:59.067 --> 00:13:01.434
a bowl of communal peanuts.

00:13:01.434 --> 00:13:03.033
Big news from Washington today

00:13:03.033 --> 00:13:05.767
as President Biden finally delivered a major update

00:13:05.767 --> 00:13:08.501
on his administration's COVID response.

00:13:08.501 --> 00:13:10.567
Yeah, just like most phone updates,

00:13:10.567 --> 00:13:12.300
Biden kept hitting "ignore" until he had no choice.

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:14.767
He was like, "Alright. Let's just update.

00:13:14.767 --> 00:13:17.734
Give me Kilimanjaro. Whatever it's called."

00:13:17.734 --> 00:13:19.601
That's right. Biden announced the U.S.

00:13:19.601 --> 00:13:22.033
will soon make high-quality masks available

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:23.400
to all Americans.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.968
And to be sure that everyone wears them,

00:13:24.968 --> 00:13:26.701
here are the new masks.

00:13:26.701 --> 00:13:28.734
It's Spidey. Yeah.

00:13:28.734 --> 00:13:30.868
Spidey. We'll all do that.

00:13:30.868 --> 00:13:32.968
That's right. We're all getting masks.

00:13:32.968 --> 00:13:36.234
Last year, we got 1,200 bucks.

00:13:36.234 --> 00:13:38.901
This year...

00:13:38.901 --> 00:13:40.267
cloth and a rubber band.

00:13:40.267 --> 00:13:42.267
Yeah, I'll take it.

00:13:42.267 --> 00:13:45.367
The White House says N95 masks are the most protective,

00:13:45.367 --> 00:13:47.767
which is too bad because I assumed the bedazzled ones

00:13:47.767 --> 00:13:51.067
I bought on Etsy were 100% COVID-proof.

00:13:51.067 --> 00:13:53.534
I washed it a couple times.

00:13:53.534 --> 00:13:55.667
Yeah, the N95 masks should be helpful.

00:13:55.667 --> 00:13:58.400
Unfortunately, out of habit, whenever somebody says, "N95,"

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.400
Biden calls it out, "Bingo!"

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.400
[ Laughter ]

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.701
[ Laughs ]

00:14:04.701 --> 00:14:06.334
That's the joke of the week.

00:14:06.334 --> 00:14:08.234
-Come on. -That's the joke of the week.

00:14:08.234 --> 00:14:10.667
That's the one.

00:14:10.667 --> 00:14:11.801
[ Chuckles ]

00:14:11.801 --> 00:14:13.234
Well, this is interesting.

00:14:13.234 --> 00:14:16.100
I read that researchers in Finland created a nasal spray

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:18.634
that they say can protect you from all COVID variants

00:14:18.634 --> 00:14:20.000
for eight hours.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.501
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:14:21.501 --> 00:14:23.334
When asked about breathing through your mouth,

00:14:23.334 --> 00:14:28.067
the company was like, "Uhh...

00:14:28.067 --> 00:14:30.567
we didn't think of that, yeah."

00:14:30.567 --> 00:14:32.968
"Oh, you're one of those people."

00:14:32.968 --> 00:14:34.434
Well, this is big news.

00:14:34.434 --> 00:14:37.000
Today, Buckingham Palace announced that Queen Elizabeth

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:41.000
has stripped Prince Andrew of all his royal affiliations.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.634
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:14:42.634 --> 00:14:44.067
That's right. She stripped Prince Andrew,

00:14:44.067 --> 00:14:46.033
making her far and away the oldest woman

00:14:46.033 --> 00:14:47.567
to ever strip Prince Andrew.

00:14:47.567 --> 00:14:49.634
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:14:49.634 --> 00:14:50.801
That might be the joke -- -Oh, that might be --

00:14:50.801 --> 00:14:52.901
That might be the joke -- -That might be --

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:55.334
-That might be the joke.

00:14:55.334 --> 00:14:58.167
-Joke of the week, week, week, week!

00:14:58.167 --> 00:15:01.534
-Go, go, go, go, go! Go, joke!

00:15:01.534 --> 00:15:04.534
[ Laughter ]

00:15:04.534 --> 00:15:06.634
Yeah, finally, a city in California

00:15:06.634 --> 00:15:09.100
wants to use green lasers to try and drive away

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:12.834
thousands of crows that have become a public nuisance.

00:15:12.834 --> 00:15:15.033
But the lasers will backfire when thousands of crows

00:15:15.033 --> 00:15:18.000
are replaced by thousands of cats.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.834
Well, guys, let's kick things off with some good news.

00:15:20.834 --> 00:15:22.300
According to a new study,

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:25.534
face masks actually make people look more attractive.

00:15:25.534 --> 00:15:27.601
[ Laughter ]

00:15:27.601 --> 00:15:29.968
So when I say this is a hot crowd, I really mean it.

00:15:29.968 --> 00:15:33.000
I mean, this is a hot crowd. That's right.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.934
You are more attractive with a mask,

00:15:34.934 --> 00:15:36.434
and you get the bonus of doing

00:15:36.434 --> 00:15:38.501
a sexy little striptease on your face.

00:15:38.501 --> 00:15:39.834
[ Laughter ]

00:15:39.834 --> 00:15:42.467
[ Sultry music plays ]

00:15:42.467 --> 00:15:44.400
Whew!

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.834
Some news from Washington.

00:15:45.834 --> 00:15:49.400
Today President Biden announced a $27-billion program

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:52.167
to repair and replace bridges across the country.

00:15:52.167 --> 00:15:54.567
So if your city is celebrating right now,

00:15:54.567 --> 00:15:58.367
you should be happy and terrified.

00:15:58.367 --> 00:16:00.834
But when Biden's staff found him looking at pictures of bridges,

00:16:00.834 --> 00:16:02.200
they were like, "Don't do it, sir!

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.000
You can't trust the poll numbers!"

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.334
Some more political news.

00:16:07.334 --> 00:16:09.100
The Republican Party said that they might not let

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:13.033
their nominees take part in future presidential debates.

00:16:13.033 --> 00:16:15.567
Instead, they want candidates to knock each other

00:16:15.567 --> 00:16:20.100
off giant rubber balls like the game show "Wipeout."

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.467
That would be too bad, if we scrap the debates.

00:16:22.467 --> 00:16:24.801
I'll miss watching 90 minutes of Chris Wallace saying,

00:16:24.801 --> 00:16:26.167
"Gentlemen, gentlemen, please.

00:16:26.167 --> 00:16:29.400
Gentlemen! Gentlemen? Gentlemen."

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.334
Seriously, it's a shame. I mean, how else are we going to

00:16:31.334 --> 00:16:33.767
get high-level political discourse like this?

00:16:33.767 --> 00:16:35.467
-Excuse me, Chris. Wait. -Number one. Number two.

00:16:35.467 --> 00:16:37.100
-Chris. -Number three.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.467
-They said it would take -- No, you were on number two.

00:16:38.467 --> 00:16:40.334
-No.

00:16:40.334 --> 00:16:41.767
[ Laughter ]

00:16:41.767 --> 00:16:43.234
-Listen to this.

00:16:43.234 --> 00:16:45.868
Apparently Walgreens and CVS are shutting down some of their

00:16:45.868 --> 00:16:48.934
pharmacies on weekends due to staffing shortages.

00:16:48.934 --> 00:16:50.400
Yeah, it's not good.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:54.901
Now when you go to CVS, there's a self-booster station.

00:16:54.901 --> 00:16:57.033
It's just a needle sticking out of the blood-pressure machine.

00:16:57.033 --> 00:16:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:16:58.767 --> 00:17:02.133
You put your arms in -- put your arms in two sleeves now.

00:17:02.133 --> 00:17:05.133
You can tell CVS values the pharmacists they do have

00:17:05.133 --> 00:17:07.467
because they keep them locked in the same plastic case

00:17:07.467 --> 00:17:10.534
as the razor blades and Sudafed.

00:17:10.534 --> 00:17:12.701
Hey, the NFL playoffs start tomorrow, and I heard

00:17:12.701 --> 00:17:15.901
that the Bills-Patriots game in Buffalo could be

00:17:15.901 --> 00:17:17.868
one of the coldest playoff games ever

00:17:17.868 --> 00:17:21.434
with a wind chill of minus-15 degrees.

00:17:21.434 --> 00:17:22.968
You'll know it's cold

00:17:22.968 --> 00:17:24.767
when the players huddle up and just stay there.

00:17:24.767 --> 00:17:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:17:27.167 --> 00:17:31.000
Meanwhile, ESPN host and former NFL linebacker Bart Scott said

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.434
the best thing for players to do before a cold-weather game --

00:17:34.434 --> 00:17:38.267
this is real -- is to take Viagra to get their --

00:17:38.267 --> 00:17:42.167
to get their blood pumping.

00:17:42.167 --> 00:17:44.434
If you go into the locker room after the game,

00:17:44.434 --> 00:17:46.934
it looks like the wand shop from Harry Potter.

00:17:46.934 --> 00:17:48.567
I'm just saying.

00:17:48.567 --> 00:17:50.567
♪♪

00:17:50.567 --> 00:17:52.567
-Abracadabra!

00:17:55.667 --> 00:17:58.100
-But remember, if the game lasts for more than four hours,

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:59.434
you gotta call your doctor.

00:17:59.434 --> 00:18:00.734
I already know that.

00:18:00.734 --> 00:18:03.000
But this is -- Thank you. But this is true.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.534
The wind chill in Buffalo could be minus 15.

00:18:05.534 --> 00:18:06.868
It's going to be freezing.

00:18:06.868 --> 00:18:08.968
Check out the signs that fans are bringing to the game.

00:18:08.968 --> 00:18:10.267
This first one says...

00:18:14.434 --> 00:18:15.968
This next one says...

00:18:19.567 --> 00:18:21.267
And finally this one says...

00:18:24.367 --> 00:18:25.968
So keep an eye out for those.

00:18:25.968 --> 00:18:29.300
[ Applause ]

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:31.200
Well, everyone's really excited about this.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.167
Today the fifth "Scream" movie hit theaters.

00:18:34.167 --> 00:18:37.200
Yeah, the franchise features the most terrifying villain --

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:40.534
someone who always calls instead of just texting.

00:18:40.534 --> 00:18:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:18:43.667 --> 00:18:46.567
Hey, I read that due to a shortage of PlayStation 5's,

00:18:46.567 --> 00:18:50.067
Sony is just going to make more PlayStation 4's.

00:18:50.067 --> 00:18:52.634
[ Laughter ]

00:18:52.634 --> 00:18:55.234
That's like the guy at Subway saying, "We ran out of new ham,

00:18:55.234 --> 00:18:57.968
so I'm just going to give you old ham."

00:18:57.968 --> 00:19:00.667
[ Laughter ]

00:19:00.667 --> 00:19:02.367
But if you have kids, here's what you do.

00:19:02.367 --> 00:19:04.434
You put the PS4 in a PS3 box.

00:19:04.434 --> 00:19:05.868
That way, they'll be disappointed

00:19:05.868 --> 00:19:07.367
but also happily surprised.

00:19:07.367 --> 00:19:09.033
[ Laughter ]

00:19:09.033 --> 00:19:11.534
And, finally, a tortoise that lives on a British island

00:19:11.534 --> 00:19:15.634
has been declared the oldest ever at 190 years old.

00:19:15.634 --> 00:19:17.801
The tortoise is so old, he takes Viagra

00:19:17.801 --> 00:19:19.801
just to get his neck out of his shell.

